hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15683","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abi Qilabah, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, he said: We came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while we were young men close in age, and we stayed with him twenty nights. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was merciful, gentle, and thought we longed for our families, so he asked us about whom we left among our families, and we informed him. So he said: Return to your families and stay among them, and teach them and order them. When prayer comes, let one of you call the call to prayer for you, then let the eldest of you lead you."
"15684","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abi Qilabah, he said: Abu Sulayman Malik ibn al-Huwayrith came to our mosque and said: By Allah, I pray, not intending prayer, but I want to show you how I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray. He said: So he sat in the first rakah when he raised his head from the last prostration, then stood."
"15685","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, that he saw the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raising his hands in his prayer when he raised his head from bowing, and when he prostrated, and when he raised his head from prostration, until he parallels with them the tops of his ears."
"15686","Ismail narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abi Qilabah, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him and to a companion of his: When prayer comes, call the call to prayer and the standing call, and once he said: then the standing call, then let the eldest of you lead you. Khalid said: So I said to Abi Qilabah: Where is recitation. He said: They were close in age."
"15687","Abu Ubaydah, meaning al-Haddad, narrated to us, he said: Aban al-Attar narrated to us, from Budayl, from Abi Atiyyah, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, he said: He visited us in our mosque. He said: Prayer was established, so they said: Lead us, may Allah have mercy on you. So he said: Let a man among you pray. So when he finished prayer he said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When a man visits a people, he shall not lead them; a man among them shall lead them."
"15688","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah al-Uqayli, he said: Abu Atiyyah, a freed slave among us, narrated to me, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, he said: He used to come to us in our prayer place, and it was said to him: Advance and pray. So he said: Let one of you pray until I tell you why I did not pray with you. When the people prayed he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you visits a people, he shall not pray with them as leader; let a man among them pray with them."
"15689","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, that he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raising his hands when he wanted to bow, and when he raised his head from bowing, and when he raised his head from prostration, until he parallels with them the tops of his ears."
